BBUUGGSS
     The ffddcc driver can interfere with other isa(4) controllers, namely some
     WD/SMC network controllers fail to work when the probing mechanism in the
     ffddcc driver probes for a missing second floppy drive.  In this case you
     should try recompiling the kernel replacing the relevant line with ffdd00 aatt
     ffddcc??.

